</mj-text>
    <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2
    style="
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin-top: 2px !important;
      margin: 0;
    "
  >
    Trump calms markets
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    <mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="REPLACE_ME"
  target="_blank"
/>
    
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What happened?</strong> Global oil prices dropped sharply after President Trump said the<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2jxe382pwo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;"> conflict with Iran could end “very soon,”</a> easing fears of prolonged war. Brent Crude, which had surged near $120 per barrel amid escalating tensions and airstrikes, fell to around $93 during trading. Markets responded positively, with global equities rebounding, including the FTSE 100, which rose at the open.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What did Trump say?</strong> Speaking at a press conference in Florida, Trump said the war was “pretty much complete” and suggested the main objective had already been achieved. However, he issued a strong warning to Iran not to disrupt shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. He said that if Iran blocks or interferes with oil flows in the strait, the US would respond with force “twenty times harder” than previous strikes.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Big picture:</strong> Comments from President Trump temporarily eased markets, but volatility is likely to persist. Even speculation about escalation can send prices sharply higher, affecting inflation, fuel expenses, and economic growth worldwide. The conflict demonstrates how geopolitical risks, energy security, and global stability remain tightly interconnected.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
