<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 0.5px 1px 1px" border-radius="5px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="5px" padding="0px">
    
    <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2
    style="
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin-top: 2px !important;
      margin: 0;
    "
  >
    Kenya budget shock
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    
    
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Summary: Kenya’s State House budget doubles, sparking debate over spending priorities and transparency.   </strong></p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What happened? </strong>Kenya’s State House budget has come under scrutiny after <a href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-kenyas-massive-state-house-budget-raises-eyebrows/a-76274407" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">supplementary estimates increased its allocation</a> to about Sh16.9B ($130M), nearly double the original Sh8.6B ($66M). Kenya’s State House budget funds State Lodges, presidential administration, travel and hospitality, and benefits for former leaders. Supplementary estimates increased the allocation to cover operational shortfalls and ongoing government activities.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Criticisms:</strong> Economists say the allocation appears excessive given the country’s rising public liabilities, pressure on government revenues, and shortages in essential sectors such as healthcare, education, and drought relief. Some analysts also question transparency, warning that minimal disclosure makes it difficult to track how the funds are actually used. Others claim the State House may be spending beyond what Parliament originally approved.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Big picture:</strong> The debate over Kenya’s State House budget reflects broader concerns about fiscal discipline and government priorities. The issue highlights a broader challenge for developing economies: balancing public spending with economic needs while avoiding perceptions of excess in government leadership.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="10px" />
    </mj-section>
    <mj-spacer height="10px" />
