          >
            Worldwide
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image
          border-radius="10px"
          padding="10px 12px"
          width="600px"
          src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
          alt="REPLACE_ME"
          href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
        />
        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇮🇳 India - No price hike.</strong> India’s government has decided not to raise petrol and diesel retail prices despite global crude oil prices rising above $100 per barrel. Officials say the policy aims to protect consumers and prevent inflation from rising sharply. State-owned oil companies, which dominate India’s fuel retail market, are expected to absorb temporary losses amid surging international prices (<a href="https://indianexpress.com/article/business/no-petrol-diesel-price-hike-despite-crude-oil-100-lpg-govt-sources-10573184/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">waiting game</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇩🇪 Germany - Exports dropped.</strong> Germany’s exports fell more than expected in January, highlighting continued weakness in Europe’s largest economy. Exports declined 2.3% month-on-month to €130.5B, slightly worse than analysts’ forecasts of a 2% drop. The decline was mainly driven by sharp reductions in shipments to China and other EU countries. Exports to China dropped by more than 13%, while exports to EU nations fell by nearly 5% (<a href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260310-german-exports-drop-in-setback-to-fragile-recovery" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">no hope</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇱🇧 Lebanon - White Phosphorous shelling.</strong> Human Rights Watch has accused Israel of unlawfully using white phosphorus munitions over residential areas in the southern Lebanese town of Yohmor. White phosphorus is typically used for smoke screens or illumination, but can also behave as an incendiary weapon, causing severe burns and fires. The Israeli military said it could not confirm the alleged use and maintained that its policy prohibits deploying such munitions (<a href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260309-hrw-accuses-israel-white-phosphorus-lebanon" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">learn more</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇧🇪 Belgium - Synagogue blast.</strong> An explosion struck a synagogue in the Belgian city of Liège, damaging the building but causing no injuries. Authorities have described the incident as an antisemitic attack targeting the Jewish community. Belgian Interior Minister Bernard Quintin condemned the explosion as a “despicable” measure and said security around Jewish sites would be strengthened. The exact cause of the explosion remains unclear (<a href="https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/09/europe/belgian-synagogue-blast-intl" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">what is happening</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
